WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.240
- This year, I've gotten
really into pro football.

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:06.150
Maybe it's getting to host the
"NFL Honors," I don't know,

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:08.910
or the fact that literally
every human that surrounds me

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:10.080
is obsessed with the game.

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:11.790
But I now am very into it,

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:14.580
and our next guest is one
of the voices of the game.

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:16.500
You can see her hosting
throughout the season

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:17.760
on NFL Network.

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:20.246
Say hello to MJ Acosta!

00:00:20.246 --> 00:00:25.246
(upbeat rhythmic music)
(audience cheering)

00:00:31.268 --> 00:00:34.152
(audience cheering continues)

00:00:34.152 --> 00:00:36.660
(upbeat rhythmic music ending)

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:38.310
So excited you're here.

00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:39.143
- Likewise.

00:00:39.143 --> 00:00:41.263
- Like I just got into it, okay?

00:00:41.263 --> 00:00:42.780
- (laughing) I know.
- Like really into...

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:44.580
Like, I'm in fantasy football too.

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:46.350
- Same, I have two leagues, it's too much.

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:48.690
- Oh, I'm gonna have more than one, yeah.

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:49.770
I... I...
(MJ gasping)

00:00:49.770 --> 00:00:51.390
- That's an undertaking,
that's a commitment.

00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:52.440
- It is an undertaking-
- Yeah.

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:54.810
- But you get so much joy,

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:57.030
and you actually start to
learn about the other teams.

00:00:57.030 --> 00:00:57.871
- [MJ Acosta] 100%.

00:00:57.871 --> 00:00:59.809
- 'Cause I used to just
only care about the Cowboys.

00:00:59.809 --> 00:01:01.080
- (laughing) Well,
which is fair, I get it,

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:01.913
it's America's team.

00:01:01.913 --> 00:01:02.746
I will say-

00:01:02.746 --> 00:01:04.071
- Thank you for saying
it, and not me, okay.

00:01:04.071 --> 00:01:04.904
(everyone laughing)

00:01:04.904 --> 00:01:06.180
- Being part of fantasy football

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:08.310
is like my sneaky trick as a sportscaster

00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:11.010
to make sure that I'm
up on every single game

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:12.180
across the entire league.

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:13.770
Because you're invested, you're in it,

00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:15.120
you get upset when you lose.

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:16.680
Which in one of my leagues, I'm abysmal,

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:18.060
and the other one, I'm crushin' it.

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:18.893
So, you know,

00:01:18.893 --> 00:01:21.000
multiple leagues does help
with the self-esteem a little.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:21.833
- Yeah.

00:01:21.833 --> 00:01:25.230
So wait, you started in broadcast
while a pro cheerleader,

00:01:25.230 --> 00:01:26.580
which I didn't actually know that.

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:27.413
- [MJ Acosta] Yeah.

00:01:27.413 --> 00:01:28.980
- That's incredible, did you
do both at the same time?

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:30.150
- Like most things in my life,

00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:33.690
I'm doing all the things
all the time, all at once.

00:01:33.690 --> 00:01:34.523
Yeah, look at that.

00:01:34.523 --> 00:01:35.356
It's so tremendous.

00:01:35.356 --> 00:01:37.530
I was already a sportscaster

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:40.590
when I made the Miami
Dolphins cheerleading team.

00:01:40.590 --> 00:01:41.423
Fun fact though,

00:01:41.423 --> 00:01:43.710
I tried out five times to be
a Miami Dolphins cheerleader

00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:45.060
before I actually made the team.

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:47.280
So tenacity, also a central theme.

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:48.149
- Yeah, yeah!

00:01:48.149 --> 00:01:49.273
(audience cheering)

00:01:49.273 --> 00:01:50.173
- Thank you.

00:01:50.173 --> 00:01:53.820
I tried out in my, not to
age myself, in my early 20s.

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:56.070
It was a very long, tedious process,

00:01:56.070 --> 00:01:57.270
made it so close every time.

00:01:57.270 --> 00:01:59.850
So I decided, let's focus,
let's focus on the career path,

00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:01.920
let's focus on other dance opportunities.

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:03.450
And even once I started my career,

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:05.767
I had this little tug at me,

00:02:05.767 --> 00:02:07.800
"If I don't try this
at least one more time

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:10.230
while I still have flexibility
early on in my career,

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:11.063
I'm gonna regret it."

00:02:11.063 --> 00:02:13.440
And sure enough, that
was the year I made it.

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:15.540
Huge advantage being on the sidelines,

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:18.570
watching the game develop
in front of me in real time,

00:02:18.570 --> 00:02:21.480
being part of a franchise,
invaluable experience

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:23.370
that still helps me to
this day in my career.

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:24.480
- [Kelly Clarkson] That's so cool!

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:25.313
- Yeah.

00:02:25.313 --> 00:02:26.146
- I never really think about that,

00:02:26.146 --> 00:02:28.050
but I think that's so cool that
yeah, you were on the field,

00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:29.970
like getting that and hearing everybody.

00:02:29.970 --> 00:02:30.803
- [MJ Acosta] 100%.

00:02:30.803 --> 00:02:32.719
- Now, you can hear people
'cause every time, it's-

00:02:32.719 --> 00:02:33.648
- [MJ Acosta] Now they're mic'd up.

00:02:33.648 --> 00:02:35.188
- "Hey, here we go!"
- Yup.

00:02:35.188 --> 00:02:36.850
You hear it all!
(audience laughing)

00:02:36.850 --> 00:02:38.446
That's a good cadence.

00:02:38.446 --> 00:02:39.279
- "Here we go!"

00:02:39.279 --> 00:02:42.630
And it's like every time
he does the play, Dak,

00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:44.550
every time, it's like a lot.

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:45.870
- It's deep in the diaphragm.

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:47.040
- Yeah, "Hey!"

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:48.300
It's every time.

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:50.130
You're gonna hear it now
if you're watchin' a game.

00:02:50.130 --> 00:02:50.963
- You could be a QB-

00:02:50.963 --> 00:02:52.845
- I love you, Dak, I love
you. (audience laughing)

00:02:52.845 --> 00:02:54.030
So I love that you also talk about this,

00:02:54.030 --> 00:02:55.680
you don't play down
your femininity at all.

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:56.513
- No, no.

00:02:56.513 --> 00:02:57.990
- 'Cause I feel like a lotta women

00:02:57.990 --> 00:02:59.400
feel like they do have to do that.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:00.233
- 100%.

00:03:00.233 --> 00:03:03.660
I think not only the industry,
and there are so many tropes.

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:05.490
And I think a big challenge
for me at the beginning

00:03:05.490 --> 00:03:08.550
was because I was an NFL
cheerleader, which by the way

00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:11.010
was one of the toughest
things I ever had to do,

00:03:11.010 --> 00:03:13.350
it was so much discipline,
so much dedication.

00:03:13.350 --> 00:03:15.150
It's one of the things
that I'm proudest of.

00:03:15.150 --> 00:03:17.617
And many folks at the
beginning of my career told me,

00:03:17.617 --> 00:03:19.470
"Yeah, you probably
shouldn't lead with that."

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:20.490
Why, when was the last time

00:03:20.490 --> 00:03:22.860
you were on the sideline
of a game the entire time?

00:03:22.860 --> 00:03:23.693
Remind me again?

00:03:23.693 --> 00:03:24.526
I didn't think so."

00:03:24.526 --> 00:03:25.359
- [Kelly Clarkson] Yeah.

00:03:25.359 --> 00:03:26.970
- And beyond that, I think-
(audience laughing)

00:03:26.970 --> 00:03:27.870
- Oh, I love you.

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:29.141
- I think you can...
(audience laughing)

00:03:29.141 --> 00:03:29.974
(laughing) Thank you, Kelly.

00:03:29.974 --> 00:03:30.807
- Yeah.

00:03:30.807 --> 00:03:33.150
- I think being hyper-feminine, or not,

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:35.730
whether you're a tomboy,
wherever you are and how you are

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:38.130
is how you should arrive
every day to work.

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:40.110
And that's very hard in sportscasting,

00:03:40.110 --> 00:03:41.940
it's very hard in just the
entertainment industry.

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:45.150
And I refused to sort of push
myself into this little box

00:03:45.150 --> 00:03:46.890
that they were constantly
trying to shove me in.

00:03:46.890 --> 00:03:48.720
It would be disingenuous, one,

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:51.240
and it would not serve
the folks who watch us,

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:52.740
who wanna see themselves reflected

00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:55.350
and wanna see themselves
represented on the screen

00:03:55.350 --> 00:03:56.490
or on social media.

00:03:56.490 --> 00:03:57.323
- [Kelly Clarkson] Yeah.

00:03:57.323 --> 00:03:59.430
- So for me, it was very
important to remind folks

00:03:59.430 --> 00:04:01.680
that I don't have to
strip away my femininity

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:04.290
to show you that I'm credible
and qualified for my job.

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:05.488
- Absolutely.

00:04:05.488 --> 00:04:06.863
(audience applauding and cheering)

00:04:06.863 --> 00:04:08.604
(audience cheering
drowning out MJ speaking)

00:04:08.604 --> 00:04:11.397
- And you're the perfect
mentor, you love mentoring.

00:04:11.397 --> 00:04:12.230
- Yes.

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:13.290
- And you're kinda the
perfect mentor to do that

00:04:13.290 --> 00:04:15.000
'cause that is like what
people need to hear,

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:16.436
especially young women in this industry.

00:04:16.436 --> 00:04:17.269
- [MJ Acosta] 100%, yeah.

00:04:17.269 --> 00:04:18.570
- That's important to
you, right, mentorship?

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:19.403
- No question.

00:04:19.403 --> 00:04:21.450
It's been one of the biggest parts

00:04:21.450 --> 00:04:23.267
of now this stage of my career.

00:04:23.267 --> 00:04:24.460
'Cause I think when I started out,

00:04:24.460 --> 00:04:27.270
there were even fewer
women than there are now.

00:04:27.270 --> 00:04:28.440
It has evolved a bit,

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:29.880
but we still have such a long way to go.

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:30.713
But there were even fewer

00:04:30.713 --> 00:04:33.510
who were really there for you step by step

00:04:33.510 --> 00:04:36.300
'cause when they started
out, they didn't have anyone.

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:38.670
So for me, it was very
important to break that cycle.

00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:40.470
And I remember at the
Super Bowl, back in Miami,

00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:42.810
which was such a beautiful
moment in my career,

00:04:42.810 --> 00:04:44.490
to be there, and to show everyone around,

00:04:44.490 --> 00:04:45.990
and to do these feature interviews-

00:04:45.990 --> 00:04:46.950
- Great merch.
- We had-

00:04:46.950 --> 00:04:47.783
- Just sayin'.

00:04:47.783 --> 00:04:48.630
- It's fantastic merch-
- Yeah, it was great merch.

00:04:48.630 --> 00:04:50.400
- The colors were phenomenal.
- Yes.

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:51.450
- We had a dinner,

00:04:51.450 --> 00:04:54.360
myself and one of my colleagues
at the NFL League office

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:56.190
put together a dinner
called A Seat at the Table.

00:04:56.190 --> 00:04:58.800
And the whole purpose of the
dinner was to create a pipeline

00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:00.960
between the women who were
already in the industry

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:02.400
and the ones who were up next.

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:04.687
To have a direct face-to-face
connection and say,

00:05:04.687 --> 00:05:07.260
"Okay, not only are we breaking
the door off the hinges,

00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:09.420
no holding it open, we're
tearin' that thing apart,

00:05:09.420 --> 00:05:12.090
but we're going to be there
with you every step of the way

00:05:12.090 --> 00:05:13.260
so you know that you're not alone.

00:05:13.260 --> 00:05:16.650
And no one understands the
challenges better than we do.

00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:18.390
We're here to navigate
and help you through,

00:05:18.390 --> 00:05:21.060
and hopefully make it a little
easier than it was for us."

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:23.370
- Yeah. And I think it's cool
too (audience applauding )

00:05:23.370 --> 00:05:25.528
'cause women more involved too.

00:05:25.528 --> 00:05:26.693
- Exactly that.

00:05:26.693 --> 00:05:29.520
- We have a young, aspiring
sports analyst here,

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:31.890
and she also has no idea that MJ is here

00:05:31.890 --> 00:05:35.280
and that MJ has a giant
surprise for her as well.

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:37.380
So MJ's gonna hide for a little bit,

00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:40.200
and we're gonna bring her
out just at the right moment.

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:43.140
So I'm gonna say bye right
now, but see you in a second.

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:44.430
At 12 years old,

00:05:44.430 --> 00:05:47.670
our next guest is the
ultimate football fanatic,

00:05:47.670 --> 00:05:49.050
so I had to have her on.

00:05:49.050 --> 00:05:51.870
She seriously doesn't
miss a single NFL game,

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:53.250
she notes every stat,

00:05:53.250 --> 00:05:56.670
and rewatches key plays
endlessly just for fun

00:05:56.670 --> 00:05:57.750
which is so cool.

00:05:57.750 --> 00:06:00.090
But for her, football
is not just a passion,

00:06:00.090 --> 00:06:01.590
she actually wants to make it a career.

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:03.418
So everybody welcome Allie.

00:06:03.418 --> 00:06:05.761
(audience cheering)

00:06:05.761 --> 00:06:06.658
Hello!

00:06:06.658 --> 00:06:07.491
- [Allie] Hi. (laughing)

00:06:07.491 --> 00:06:09.240
- So I'm recently in love with football,

00:06:09.240 --> 00:06:11.250
so you're gonna know way more than me,

00:06:11.250 --> 00:06:13.470
but I'm so excited about it.
(Allie laughing)

00:06:13.470 --> 00:06:15.930
So wait, so what's your favorite team?

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:18.330
- My favorite team is
the Kansas City Chiefs.

00:06:18.330 --> 00:06:20.550
- Oh, that's a good one. Okay,
they have great initials.

00:06:20.550 --> 00:06:21.821
Yes, I like them.

00:06:21.821 --> 00:06:22.830
(Allie and audience laughing)

00:06:22.830 --> 00:06:25.290
No, mine's the Cowboys, I love the Cow...

00:06:25.290 --> 00:06:26.962
Don't you look at me like that, girl!

00:06:26.962 --> 00:06:28.110
(audience laughing)

00:06:28.110 --> 00:06:29.400
I love them so much!

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:30.360
But no, I'm gonna say Mahomes,

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:31.488
is he one of your favorites?

00:06:31.488 --> 00:06:32.501
- Yes, definitely one of my favorites.

00:06:32.501 --> 00:06:33.334
- He's really good.

00:06:33.334 --> 00:06:35.220
Yeah, I would say he's
pretty talented, yeah.

00:06:35.220 --> 00:06:37.800
So wait, do you wanna make
football like a career?

00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:39.750
- Definitely, absolutely, yeah. (laughing)

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:41.790
- And you wanna do like broadcasting,

00:06:41.790 --> 00:06:43.470
like what do you wanna do?

00:06:43.470 --> 00:06:46.890
- I feel like it can really
depend on each day, (laughing)

00:06:46.890 --> 00:06:49.830
I kinda feel like I wanna
do something different.

00:06:49.830 --> 00:06:52.140
I love watching the "New Heights" podcast,

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:53.220
the Kelce brothers.

00:06:53.220 --> 00:06:54.565
I think they're great.
- Oh yeah.

00:06:54.565 --> 00:06:55.398
They're hilarious, yeah.

00:06:55.398 --> 00:06:56.473
- Yeah, I love them. (laughing)

00:06:56.473 --> 00:06:57.420
- [Kelly Clarkson] Yeah.

00:06:57.420 --> 00:06:59.100
- So something like that,

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:01.950
like watching and analyzing the game,

00:07:01.950 --> 00:07:04.260
and giving facts and background knowledge

00:07:04.260 --> 00:07:07.440
to people who aren't the
biggest fans of football

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:09.270
or who don't know
football incredibly well,

00:07:09.270 --> 00:07:10.103
just making it accessible.
- Me,

00:07:10.103 --> 00:07:11.127
I love people like you, yeah.

00:07:11.127 --> 00:07:12.690
And you inform us, yes,

00:07:12.690 --> 00:07:14.310
that's why I love listening
to the commentators,

00:07:14.310 --> 00:07:17.520
the analysts, like all
that because I'm new to it.

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:19.140
- Yeah.
- So it's a really cool thing

00:07:19.140 --> 00:07:21.540
'cause then you get to bring
new people into the sport.

00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:23.060
- Definitely, yes. (laughing)
- Yeah.

00:07:23.060 --> 00:07:25.530
So I know that you're
early in your career path,

00:07:25.530 --> 00:07:27.060
but we have someone here

00:07:27.060 --> 00:07:29.670
who's as passionate about
sports broadcasting as you are.

00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:32.190
So, she wanted to meet you
'cause she's very impressed.

00:07:32.190 --> 00:07:34.650
So she's an Emmy-winning sportscaster,

00:07:34.650 --> 00:07:36.994
and to us, she is a
whole lotta woman, y'all.

00:07:36.994 --> 00:07:40.956
(exciting rhythmic music)
(audience cheering)

00:07:40.956 --> 00:07:43.380
Okay, so say hello to MJ Acosta!

00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:44.295
(audience cheering)

00:07:44.295 --> 00:07:45.598
Look at her!

00:07:45.598 --> 00:07:49.472
(exciting rhythmic music continues)

00:07:49.472 --> 00:07:51.255
She said, "What?"

00:07:51.255 --> 00:07:52.272
- Oh my gosh!

00:07:52.272 --> 00:07:53.962
(exciting rhythmic music ending)

00:07:53.962 --> 00:07:56.100
(audience cheering)

00:07:56.100 --> 00:07:57.560
I think you're amazing. (laughing)

00:07:57.560 --> 00:07:59.310
- Aw, I think you're amazing.
(Allie laughing)

00:07:59.310 --> 00:08:00.143
- Y'all, have a seat!

00:08:00.143 --> 00:08:01.310
- Yes, please!

00:08:02.340 --> 00:08:04.230
- Oh my... Good surprise, good surprise?

00:08:04.230 --> 00:08:05.145
- Yeah. (laughing)

00:08:05.145 --> 00:08:05.978
- Yeah?

00:08:05.978 --> 00:08:06.811
(audience laughing)

00:08:06.811 --> 00:08:08.250
She's doin' something you
might wanna be doin' later.

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:09.083
- Yeah. (laughing)

00:08:09.083 --> 00:08:09.960
- What impresses you most about this one?

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:12.240
- Ugh, first of all,
I'm already a huge fan.

00:08:12.240 --> 00:08:13.073
Another curlfriend,

00:08:13.073 --> 00:08:14.940
we need more of us out here.
- (laughing) Yes.

00:08:14.940 --> 00:08:15.773
- I think just the fact

00:08:15.773 --> 00:08:17.310
that you love the game so much already.

00:08:17.310 --> 00:08:21.930
You're already a fan of it,
but also an analyst at it too.

00:08:21.930 --> 00:08:24.030
So even if you're not
on television, right,

00:08:24.030 --> 00:08:26.850
the fact that you're in
it is already a huge step.

00:08:26.850 --> 00:08:28.710
